// NDepend issue suppressions for the whole solution (NDepend reads assembly-level
// SuppressMessage attributes from any analysed assembly, so this one file covers all projects).
//
// Keep this file short. Order of preference when NDepend reports something:
//   1. fix the code;
//   2. fix the rule or the JustMyCode definition in Stride.CommunityToolkit.ndproj
//      (generated code such as Stride.Core.DataSerializers and UpdateEngineAutoGenerated
//      is excluded there, not here);
//   3. only then add a targeted suppression below, with a real justification.
//
// Target format is "AssemblyName:CodeElementFullName" - the assembly prefix is mandatory,
// wildcards are not supported. A suppression silently does nothing once its target is gone,
// so prune entries when examples are removed.

using System.Diagnostics.CodeAnalysis;

